# WEFES NEXUS NEPAL: CURSOR AI GOVERNANCE & BEHAVIOR RULES
# ==============================================================================
# MANDATORY COMPLIANCE FOR CURSOR AI & DEVELOPERS
# ==============================================================================

You are working on the Water-Energy-Food-Ecosystem-Society (WEFES) Nexus Nepal platform for Gulmi District.
Because regional policy, agriculture, and water resource allocations depend on this platform, DATA TRUTH AND SCIENTIFIC RIGOR ARE ABSOLUTE PRIORITY #1.

## 1. ABSOLUTE ZERO-SYNTHESIS IN `data/real/`
- NEVER fabricate, mock, estimate, or synthesize data records inside `data/real/`.
- `data/real/` is an IMMUTABLE, READ-ONLY tier reserved exclusively for official government records (DHM, MoALD, CBS, Survey Department, NASA POWER).
- If a cited data file does not physically exist on disk:
  - DO NOT generate a stub or synthetic file to "fix" the reference.
  - DO NOT invent numbers or discharge values.
  - STOP and identify the true ground-truth file already present on disk (or update the citation to point to the actual canonical file).

## 2. PHYSICAL DISK VERIFICATION REQUIREMENT
- Before writing any citation string (`dataSourceCitation`), in-code provenance block (`// [DATA PROVENANCE]`), or import statement:
  - Verify that the referenced file physically exists on disk.
  - Never assume a file exists based on markdown examples or conventions.

## 3. ENGINE ISOLATION (ZERO INWARD IMPORTS)
- Code under `engines/` must NEVER import anything from `apps/` or `packages/`.
- Engines (`engines/water/hydro`, `engines/nexus`) are headless, autonomous computational models.
- Communication occurs strictly via CLI arguments, environment variables, or clean file artifacts (GeoJSON, CSV, JSON).

## 4. ZERO HARDCODED CONSTANTS
- Scientific numbers, coordinates, percentages, crop coefficients, and tariff estimates must NEVER be hardcoded into component or script files.
- All domain parameters must be loaded from canonical files in `data/`.

## 5. GIT HYGIENE & ATOMIC COMMITS
- Net functional code changes per commit must NOT exceed 400 lines.
- Never push directly to `main`. Always work on dedicated feature branches.
- Always ensure `python3 scripts/verify_data_integrity.py` passes.
